  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Widespread showers and widely scattered \nthunderstorms will develop today, with drying conditions \nreturning for the early half of the coming week.\n\nApproaching upper shortwave energy should allow the boundary\nthat was near the VA/NC border this morning to lift northward as\na warm front along with increased deep layer moisture. Some\nconvective initiation has already occurred with some scattered\nshowers pushing northward in the CWA. Coverage should increase\nlater this afternoon and evening as the upper forcing kicks in\nmore. Morning stratus lingered on for a while so destabilization\ncould be limited - progged MLCAPE is around 1000 J/kg and the  \nmorning sounding indicated some tall skinny CAPE profile. Shear\nparameters are weak so all in all any thunderstorms should be\nyour generic garden variety but possible training could lead to\nsome localized flooding. A few strong storms could be possible\nfrom downburst winds. Decent coverage could last through the\nevening and there is some CAM consensus on this. Trough axis\nshould make it's way into the area by Sunday morning and allow\nfor a mostly dry second half of the weekend. \n\nA weak cold front should push southward across the area for\nMonday though this should be mainly a dry passage and with a\nridge building in behind this feature at least the first half \nof the work week looks to remain dry as well.",
